* Why Values Are the First Thing You Understand
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-03 Thu 15:23
:ARCHIVE_FILE: ~/Projects/hugo-projects/vhmp-site/content-org/programming-fundamentals.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Values/Values
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: programming-fundamentals
:END:
There is no way to directly represent what a value is in any programming language. One might say that in programming language X, I can make a variable that is assigned a value. While that is functionally accurate, a value is more so an idea of the kind of information a computer can store, pass around, choose, remove, etc.

* Data Types
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-09-03 Thu 17:57
:ARCHIVE_FILE: ~/Projects/hugo-projects/vhmp-site/content-org/programming-fundamentals.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Data Types
